1
00:00:00,470 --> 00:00:01,770
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:01,770 --> 00:00:03,540
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,540 --> 00:00:05,210
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:07,110 --> 00:00:08,380
(Episode 30)

5
00:00:22,230 --> 00:00:24,100
Isn't she Joo Mi Ran?

6
00:00:24,160 --> 00:00:25,660
Joo Mi Ran!

7
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:27,970
I mean, Joo Ae Sook!

8
00:00:33,670 --> 00:00:35,910
You know Park Hee Jung, right?

9
00:00:35,910 --> 00:00:37,140
She was my daughter-in-law and...

10
00:00:37,210 --> 00:00:38,940
I told you
that you can't do this here.

11
00:00:39,010 --> 00:00:40,410
- But...
- Ma'am, I'm sorry.

12
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:42,380
No, that's not it.

13
00:00:42,450 --> 00:00:43,780
My daughter-in-law
took your daughter...

14
00:00:43,850 --> 00:00:45,280
- Come on.
- Wait, why?

15
00:00:45,350 --> 00:00:48,290
Just leave me be. Unbelievable.

16
00:00:48,350 --> 00:00:50,020
I said let go of me.

17
00:00:50,090 --> 00:00:52,020
What's the matter with you?

18
00:00:52,090 --> 00:00:54,830
Leave me be. Let go of me!

19
00:00:54,960 --> 00:00:57,030
Seriously.
You just don't know any better.

20
00:00:58,900 --> 00:01:00,570
- What's going on?
- Let go!

21
00:01:00,630 --> 00:01:01,630
Is she someone you know?

22
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:03,770
No, she must have been mistaken.

23
00:01:04,300 --> 00:01:06,240
Is this the best security can do?

24
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:09,440
Could she be a stalker
or something, too?

25
00:01:10,010 --> 00:01:11,010
My gosh.

26
00:01:12,480 --> 00:01:14,080
I doubt it.

27
00:01:14,380 --> 00:01:16,210
Why worry when I'm here?

28
00:01:17,980 --> 00:01:19,680
- Let's go.
- Okay.

29
00:01:23,390 --> 00:01:27,630
(Maternity Handbook)

30
00:01:35,230 --> 00:01:38,300
(Maternity Handbook)

31
00:01:41,470 --> 00:01:42,870
(Mother's Name: Joo Ae Sook,
Baby girl, DOB: September 11, 2000)

32
00:01:42,870 --> 00:01:44,310
(Mother's Name: Joo Ae Sook)

33
00:01:50,320 --> 00:01:52,950
(Maternity Handbook)

34
00:01:53,020 --> 00:01:56,490
(Cheongma Scholarship Foundation,
PR Director Joo Mi Ran)

35
00:01:57,960 --> 00:01:59,160
You know Park Hee Jung, right?

36
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:00,360
She was my daughter-in-law and...

37
00:02:00,430 --> 00:02:02,060
I told you
that you can't do this here.

38
00:02:02,130 --> 00:02:03,500
- But...
- Ma'am, I'm sorry.

39
00:02:03,560 --> 00:02:05,530
No, that's not it.

40
00:02:05,600 --> 00:02:07,000
My daughter-in-law
took your daughter...

41
00:02:07,070 --> 00:02:08,470
- Come on.
- Wait, why?

42
00:02:09,030 --> 00:02:10,100
Park Hee Jung,

43
00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:13,440
you finally brought trouble my way.

44
00:02:14,810 --> 00:02:17,980
You're still dragging me down
even after you're dead?

45
00:02:18,140 --> 00:02:19,480
You absolute parasite.

46
00:02:30,490 --> 00:02:31,620
It's me.

47
00:02:32,220 --> 00:02:33,830
Take care of something quickly
for me.

48
00:02:35,460 --> 00:02:38,600
Joo Ae Sook, are you trying
to wriggle out of this?

49
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:40,470
From the looks of it,

50
00:02:40,470 --> 00:02:42,330
she's definitely
Eun Seol's biological mother.

51
00:02:43,470 --> 00:02:47,110
She was clearly trembling with fear.

52
00:02:47,370 --> 00:02:48,370
Hold on.

53
00:02:49,370 --> 00:02:50,510
The handbook...

54
00:02:51,040 --> 00:02:54,610
How could she possibly back out
when I have the handbook?

55
00:02:54,950 --> 00:02:56,480
I have undeniable proof.

56
00:02:57,220 --> 00:02:58,250
Hold on.

57
00:02:59,050 --> 00:03:01,520
Wait, why isn't it here?

58
00:03:02,250 --> 00:03:04,790
Hold on, the maternity handbook.

59
00:03:04,820 --> 00:03:06,820
Where's the maternity handbook?

60
00:03:07,430 --> 00:03:11,000
I definitely put it in here.
Where is it?

61
00:03:11,060 --> 00:03:12,330
So,

62
00:03:12,900 --> 00:03:17,370
you want me to create a person
named Joo Ae Sook, right?

63
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:20,540
Set it up with a strong actor.

64
00:03:20,610 --> 00:03:23,940
There are plenty of people like that
around me.

65
00:03:24,310 --> 00:03:26,140
Including myself, of course.

66
00:03:26,510 --> 00:03:29,880
You see,
for people who backstab others,

67
00:03:29,950 --> 00:03:32,250
acting skills are essential.

68
00:03:33,750 --> 00:03:35,890
Even if it is acting,
it needs to be realistic.

69
00:03:36,390 --> 00:03:39,820
She has to look like someone
who's been through a lot.

70
00:03:39,920 --> 00:03:41,490
You don't have to remind me.

71
00:03:41,960 --> 00:03:45,460
After all, are we not experts
in that field?

72
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:54,110
Thank you so much, Team Leader Seo.

73
00:03:54,410 --> 00:03:57,910
I know I asked for a sudden review
of the new scholarship program,

74
00:03:58,310 --> 00:04:00,650
but you organized everything
so meticulously.

75
00:04:02,480 --> 00:04:03,550
Don't mention it.

76
00:04:03,720 --> 00:04:05,720
Since it's a public interest
scholarship program funded...

77
00:04:05,720 --> 00:04:07,720
by the Cheongma
Scholarship Foundation,

78
00:04:07,790 --> 00:04:10,660
I had to carefully check
for any legal risks.

79
00:04:11,090 --> 00:04:13,390
Besides, it's a project
you and dear Eun Seol...

80
00:04:13,460 --> 00:04:14,830
are personally leading.

81
00:04:14,830 --> 00:04:16,260
Of course I should help.

82
00:04:19,830 --> 00:04:22,400
"Dear" Eun Seol?

83
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:26,240
Gosh, no.

84
00:04:26,300 --> 00:04:28,840
I didn't mean it the way you think.

85
00:04:29,310 --> 00:04:31,710
You and Eun Seol...

86
00:04:31,780 --> 00:04:33,810
must share a special bond.

87
00:04:34,250 --> 00:04:36,210
I didn't know until today.

88
00:04:37,250 --> 00:04:41,750
He helped me a lot
through some difficult times.

89
00:04:42,390 --> 00:04:43,660
I see.

90
00:04:44,820 --> 00:04:48,630
Knowing that a good person like you
is by Eun Seol's side...

91
00:04:48,630 --> 00:04:50,560
gives me peace of mind.

92
00:04:51,830 --> 00:04:56,230
Please continue to take good care
of our Eun Seol in the future.

93
00:04:57,600 --> 00:05:00,540
Of course.
I should always watch over her.

94
00:05:09,210 --> 00:05:12,820
Mr. Seo seems like
a truly good person.

95
00:05:14,450 --> 00:05:17,390
I always thought
he was a good person,

96
00:05:18,160 --> 00:05:20,560
but I saw him
in a whole new light this time.

97
00:05:21,830 --> 00:05:23,090
Since it was for you,

98
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:25,930
it felt like
he went out of his way to help.

99
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:28,530
I'm always so grateful
for all his help.

100
00:05:28,830 --> 00:05:30,400
Having him at Cheongma...

101
00:05:30,470 --> 00:05:32,770
made it much easier for me to adapt.

102
00:05:32,770 --> 00:05:34,310
Exactly.

103
00:05:34,470 --> 00:05:39,180
I'm so relieved that someone
as kind as him is...

104
00:05:39,240 --> 00:05:40,980
by your side.

105
00:05:42,880 --> 00:05:46,820
The more I live, the more I realize
that people with scars...

106
00:05:46,920 --> 00:05:49,220
need someone warm in their lives.

107
00:05:50,590 --> 00:05:54,330
Because warmth like that
always spreads to others.

108
00:05:56,230 --> 00:05:57,230
I see.

109
00:05:59,730 --> 00:06:03,700
For the record,
I'm all for office romances.

110
00:06:04,870 --> 00:06:08,540
Even Hae Ra is having
an office romance with Chief Cha.

111
00:06:10,810 --> 00:06:13,710
So, if you have feelings
for someone,

112
00:06:13,780 --> 00:06:17,380
don't hold back
and express them fully.

113
00:06:22,920 --> 00:06:24,890
With guards blocking the entrance,

114
00:06:24,960 --> 00:06:27,990
how am I even supposed
to reach Joo Ae Sook?

115
00:06:29,690 --> 00:06:30,960
Is there a back door somewhere?

116
00:06:32,360 --> 00:06:35,170
Would a building that big
only have one entrance?

117
00:06:36,530 --> 00:06:40,710
There has to be a hole somewhere,
so I can squeeze my way in.

118
00:06:40,970 --> 00:06:43,210
- A hole somewhere?
- Oh my, you startled me.

119
00:06:45,380 --> 00:06:48,210
Why would you be looking
for a back entrance?

120
00:06:48,280 --> 00:06:50,680
- It's nothing.
- It does not look like nothing.

121
00:06:51,180 --> 00:06:52,980
Just tell me. What's going on?

122
00:06:54,050 --> 00:06:55,720
What do you mean?

123
00:06:55,720 --> 00:06:58,160
Well, old Mr. Park...

124
00:06:58,220 --> 00:07:01,830
has been cheating at cards every day
at the senior center,

125
00:07:02,330 --> 00:07:05,260
so I was thinking of sneaking in
to catch him.

126
00:07:05,430 --> 00:07:06,500
Really?

127
00:07:06,760 --> 00:07:09,270
The one who cheats at cards
is you, Mom.

128
00:07:09,500 --> 00:07:11,540
That's why everyone
at the senior center...

129
00:07:11,600 --> 00:07:13,270
kicked you out last time.

130
00:07:13,340 --> 00:07:14,370
I told you I didn't cheat!

131
00:07:15,570 --> 00:07:18,910
You never believe your mother,
even when it's the truth, do you?

132
00:07:19,480 --> 00:07:22,380
I could trust anyone else,

133
00:07:22,450 --> 00:07:24,480
but I always doubt what you tell me.

134
00:07:24,920 --> 00:07:29,290
Even though we're family,
I can't make excuses for your lying.

135
00:07:29,290 --> 00:07:31,090
You've got to stop doing it.

136
00:07:32,090 --> 00:07:36,630
Fine, you brat. Believe it or don't.

137
00:07:36,690 --> 00:07:37,700
What?

138
00:07:38,630 --> 00:07:39,730
Darn it.

139
00:07:39,800 --> 00:07:42,830
What kind of trouble
is she trying to stir up now?

140
00:07:43,370 --> 00:07:44,670
(Park Hee Jung, Lee Seon Mi)

141
00:07:51,880 --> 00:07:53,850
(Park Hee Jung, Lee Seon Mi)

142
00:07:55,250 --> 00:07:57,320
I can't believe
she's taking it this far.

143
00:07:59,680 --> 00:08:01,050
I'm home.

144
00:08:01,720 --> 00:08:03,490
Hey, Mr. Seok Jin.

145
00:08:05,820 --> 00:08:06,920
What are you doing?

146
00:08:06,920 --> 00:08:10,800
I've been texting that nice lady.

147
00:08:10,830 --> 00:08:13,130
The nice lady?
How did you get her number?

148
00:08:13,400 --> 00:08:17,570
She saved it on my phone
when she visited me at the hospital.

149
00:08:17,600 --> 00:08:18,670
Did she?

150
00:08:19,440 --> 00:08:21,910
Still, don't bother her so much.

151
00:08:21,970 --> 00:08:23,670
She must be tired too.

152
00:08:23,940 --> 00:08:27,510
But I'm having fun.
She likes me too, you know.

153
00:08:29,880 --> 00:08:32,250
Mom, you're not listening to me
at all these days.

154
00:08:33,480 --> 00:08:36,220
Ms. So Yeon,
why have you changed so much?

155
00:08:36,490 --> 00:08:38,190
You're upsetting me.

156
00:08:38,360 --> 00:08:41,630
All right, fine. I hear you.

157
00:08:41,690 --> 00:08:46,460
I'll do as you say
and stop texting her for today.

158
00:08:46,530 --> 00:08:50,030
There. So don't be upset, okay?

159
00:08:50,100 --> 00:08:51,570
Now that sounds like my mom.

160
00:08:52,800 --> 00:08:55,370
I listen to you very well,
Mr. Seok Jin.

161
00:08:56,810 --> 00:08:57,880
Yes, you do.

162
00:08:58,340 --> 00:09:01,780
By the way, will your shoe store...

163
00:09:01,850 --> 00:09:03,810
be opening soon?

164
00:09:04,780 --> 00:09:05,820
Yes.

165
00:09:06,120 --> 00:09:08,090
The opening ceremony
for your son's new brand...

166
00:09:08,150 --> 00:09:09,490
is happening soon.

167
00:09:09,650 --> 00:09:12,120
I'd like to go see it as well.

168
00:09:13,560 --> 00:09:14,630
You want to come see it?

169
00:09:14,890 --> 00:09:15,890
Yes.

170
00:09:15,960 --> 00:09:19,300
I want to check out your shoe store.

171
00:09:19,630 --> 00:09:22,870
Well, maybe next time.

172
00:09:23,300 --> 00:09:26,040
The grand opening will be
too crowded and noisy.

173
00:09:26,040 --> 00:09:28,170
You hate loud noises, Mom.

174
00:09:28,240 --> 00:09:32,810
But there, I'll get to see
the nice lady again.

175
00:09:33,410 --> 00:09:35,750
I really want to go.

176
00:09:36,010 --> 00:09:38,220
You just want to see
the nice lady, don't you?

177
00:09:39,520 --> 00:09:43,090
Yes, I really want to see her again.

178
00:09:44,660 --> 00:09:48,490
Then why don't you just meet
the nice lady separately?

179
00:09:49,890 --> 00:09:52,960
Really? Can I really do that?

180
00:09:53,660 --> 00:09:56,970
I want to eat
delicious food with her...

181
00:09:57,030 --> 00:09:58,700
and hang out with her.

182
00:10:17,920 --> 00:10:19,720
(Cheongma)

183
00:10:23,330 --> 00:10:24,700
Are the preparations going well?

184
00:10:25,400 --> 00:10:26,430
Yes.

185
00:10:26,760 --> 00:10:28,930
The Design Team is helping out
at the store, right?

186
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:30,770
Yes, they're getting prepared.

187
00:10:31,900 --> 00:10:33,840
Make sure to check
the VIP list carefully.

188
00:10:33,900 --> 00:10:35,370
I checked it multiple times.

189
00:10:38,810 --> 00:10:39,940
By the way,

190
00:10:40,710 --> 00:10:42,380
Ms. Park isn't coming today, right?

191
00:10:44,580 --> 00:10:45,850
I mean, it's fine if she comes,

192
00:10:45,920 --> 00:10:47,820
but I'm afraid
she'll get overwhelmed.

193
00:10:48,190 --> 00:10:50,760
You know how anxious she gets
when it's crowded.

194
00:10:51,390 --> 00:10:53,390
I told her to come next time.

195
00:10:53,490 --> 00:10:54,990
I'm glad you did.

196
00:10:55,360 --> 00:10:56,830
I was actually worried.

197
00:10:56,990 --> 00:11:00,130
We don't want rumors starting
while reporters are around.

198
00:11:03,900 --> 00:11:05,040
What rumors?

199
00:11:05,400 --> 00:11:06,440
I mean,

200
00:11:06,600 --> 00:11:10,010
it won't be good for your image
or the brand's reputation.

201
00:11:10,780 --> 00:11:13,440
What exactly do you think of my mom?

202
00:11:13,940 --> 00:11:15,510
What do you mean?

203
00:11:15,780 --> 00:11:19,450
I think of her as a mother-in-law
who needs a whole lot of help.

204
00:11:20,990 --> 00:11:22,420
Can't I even say that much?

205
00:11:24,160 --> 00:11:25,890
Whatever.
I'll see you at the store later.

206
00:11:37,840 --> 00:11:38,940
To be honest,

207
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:41,140
the opening ceremony today
kept me up all night.

208
00:11:41,140 --> 00:11:42,740
- Really?
- Yes.

209
00:11:42,810 --> 00:11:44,210
- Because you were excited?
- Yes.

210
00:12:04,700 --> 00:12:05,830
Wait, this place...

211
00:12:06,530 --> 00:12:08,030
It's where Eun Seol works.

212
00:12:09,030 --> 00:12:10,170
Why did she come here?

213
00:12:14,740 --> 00:12:16,440
Anyway, you can't go in.

214
00:12:16,910 --> 00:12:19,510
- Solicitors aren't allowed.
- What?

215
00:12:19,740 --> 00:12:21,150
A solicitor?

216
00:12:21,580 --> 00:12:24,650
- You think I'm a solicitor?
- Fine, whatever.

217
00:12:24,720 --> 00:12:26,880
- Just leave.
- Are you kidding me?

218
00:12:26,950 --> 00:12:28,650
- Please leave.
- Hey, let go!

219
00:12:29,990 --> 00:12:32,120
Why are you pushing
an elderly person?

220
00:12:32,190 --> 00:12:34,560
You... Why are you here?

221
00:12:34,990 --> 00:12:35,990
What about you, Mom?

222
00:12:36,060 --> 00:12:38,130
Why did you come
to Eun Seol's workplace?

223
00:12:38,200 --> 00:12:40,360
That's beside the point right now.

224
00:12:40,430 --> 00:12:41,970
That woman is here.

225
00:12:42,400 --> 00:12:44,100
- What?
- Seriously?

226
00:12:44,100 --> 00:12:47,340
Don't do this here,
and please leave.

227
00:12:47,400 --> 00:12:48,840
I'm a very important person.

228
00:12:48,840 --> 00:12:50,210
- Don't push.
- I'm not leaving.

229
00:12:50,210 --> 00:12:52,040
- I won't leave.
- Don't push us.

230
00:12:52,040 --> 00:12:53,310
Seriously?

231
00:12:53,880 --> 00:12:56,450
- I will claim damages.
- Go ahead. Please do.

232
00:12:56,510 --> 00:12:58,750
- Wait, don't push.
- That's enough.

233
00:13:01,690 --> 00:13:03,050
You said you know me?

234
00:13:05,920 --> 00:13:07,120
Follow me then.

235
00:13:07,830 --> 00:13:08,930
It's fine.

236
00:13:14,630 --> 00:13:16,530
Gosh, you're a mess.

237
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:19,740
Would it've killed you
to dress up a bit?

238
00:13:19,800 --> 00:13:20,800
Unbelievable.

239
00:13:22,640 --> 00:13:25,210
- Who is she?
- Who do you think?

240
00:13:25,280 --> 00:13:26,710
She's Eun Seol's mom.

241
00:13:27,910 --> 00:13:29,810
- What?
- Half a million dollars.

242
00:13:30,210 --> 00:13:32,950
That's 100,000 dollars times 5.
Come on.

243
00:13:33,820 --> 00:13:34,820
But...

244
00:13:38,960 --> 00:13:41,960
I was actually going
to contact you anyway.

245
00:13:42,330 --> 00:13:43,530
Is that so?

246
00:13:43,830 --> 00:13:45,730
After turning someone away
like that,

247
00:13:45,730 --> 00:13:48,200
you obviously should've gotten
in touch.

248
00:13:49,770 --> 00:13:50,970
So,

249
00:13:51,040 --> 00:13:54,040
does Eun Seol know?

250
00:13:55,070 --> 00:13:57,110
- Know what?
- That you are...

251
00:13:57,510 --> 00:13:59,810
her biological mother.

252
00:14:01,250 --> 00:14:03,310
You must be mistaken.

253
00:14:03,580 --> 00:14:05,750
I'm not Ko Eun Seol's
biological mother.

254
00:14:06,280 --> 00:14:07,790
What are you talking about?

255
00:14:08,190 --> 00:14:11,460
You are Joo Ae Sook, are you not?

256
00:14:12,490 --> 00:14:14,360
Yes, I am.

257
00:14:15,190 --> 00:14:16,290
However,

258
00:14:16,330 --> 00:14:19,230
the Joo Ae Sook you are looking for
is a different person.

259
00:14:19,500 --> 00:14:21,630
Wait, what do you mean?

260
00:14:22,430 --> 00:14:24,800
You must have been confused
because we share the same name.

261
00:14:25,470 --> 00:14:28,370
This is the address of
the Joo Ae Sook you are looking for.

262
00:14:28,840 --> 00:14:29,840
What?

263
00:14:31,110 --> 00:14:32,410
Is this...

264
00:14:33,240 --> 00:14:35,810
where Eun Seol's mom lives?

265
00:14:35,880 --> 00:14:38,380
She probably wasn't in the yearbook.

266
00:14:38,450 --> 00:14:40,220
She didn't graduate.

267
00:14:40,220 --> 00:14:41,650
That can't be right.

268
00:14:42,450 --> 00:14:45,490
How could there be two Joo Ae Sooks?

269
00:14:45,960 --> 00:14:48,130
There were so many students
back then,

270
00:14:48,190 --> 00:14:50,330
so it was common for kids
to have the same name.

271
00:14:52,060 --> 00:14:53,800
- What...
- Gosh, I'm so sorry.

272
00:14:53,830 --> 00:14:56,330
We must've been misinformed
and made a mistake.

273
00:14:56,700 --> 00:14:58,740
Mom, what are you doing?
Apologize to her.

274
00:14:58,800 --> 00:15:00,100
No way.

275
00:15:00,800 --> 00:15:04,310
Are you really
not Eun Seol's mother?

276
00:15:05,740 --> 00:15:08,810
I feel very sorry about
what happened to Hee Jung.

277
00:15:09,350 --> 00:15:10,710
That is why the company...

278
00:15:10,780 --> 00:15:13,380
is taking special care
of Ko Eun Seol.

279
00:15:13,450 --> 00:15:16,590
You must be someone
helping our Eun Seol.

280
00:15:17,020 --> 00:15:18,020
Goodness.

281
00:15:19,290 --> 00:15:21,760
Please take good care of her.

282
00:15:21,990 --> 00:15:25,300
She has been through so much
since she was young...

283
00:15:25,360 --> 00:15:26,830
which worries me a bit,

284
00:15:26,900 --> 00:15:29,800
but she's very hardworking
and brave.

285
00:15:29,870 --> 00:15:32,040
If you just look out for her
a little,

286
00:15:32,400 --> 00:15:35,010
she will never forget your kindness
and will surely repay you.

287
00:15:36,070 --> 00:15:39,540
She's doing a lot better
than you worry about.

288
00:15:42,280 --> 00:15:45,220
The Joo Ae Sook we're looking for
lives here?

289
00:15:45,550 --> 00:15:48,120
I think we took up
too much of your time.

290
00:15:48,190 --> 00:15:49,820
Mom, get up.

291
00:15:51,320 --> 00:15:53,890
- Come on, let's go.
- Why are you rushing me?

292
00:15:53,960 --> 00:15:55,190
We're so sorry.

293
00:15:56,060 --> 00:15:57,330
Come on.

294
00:15:57,530 --> 00:15:58,730
- We'll leave you to it.
- Right.

295
00:16:03,930 --> 00:16:05,700
I'm so sorry about this.

296
00:16:14,850 --> 00:16:19,280
Can't you tell from the address?
It's obviously some slum.

297
00:16:20,680 --> 00:16:21,990
Seriously, Mom.

298
00:16:22,320 --> 00:16:24,790
Did you think Eun Seol's bio mom
was some kind of lottery ticket?

299
00:16:27,460 --> 00:16:28,790
Now that we know,

300
00:16:29,930 --> 00:16:31,700
we should go visit her.

301
00:16:32,330 --> 00:16:34,630
Forget it. You go by yourself.

302
00:16:35,900 --> 00:16:38,940
Half a million dollars, my foot.

303
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:42,110
Judging by the address,
she couldn't even pay 500 dollars.

304
00:16:42,170 --> 00:16:43,240
Still...

305
00:16:43,610 --> 00:16:48,050
Don't tell Eun Seol just yet.
Don't say a single word.

306
00:16:48,110 --> 00:16:49,550
I wouldn't even if you told me to.

307
00:16:50,210 --> 00:16:52,280
Goodness, I'm drained.

308
00:16:54,250 --> 00:16:56,990
I wouldn't tell her
even if I were paid to.

309
00:16:57,520 --> 00:17:01,930
Just kill me already.

310
00:17:02,990 --> 00:17:06,400
My half a million dollars.

311
00:17:06,960 --> 00:17:12,540
Half a million dollars,
will I see you in my next life?

312
00:17:12,840 --> 00:17:15,170
My half a million dollars.

313
00:17:20,280 --> 00:17:23,110
From now on,
we'll have packed meals for lunch.

314
00:17:23,550 --> 00:17:24,550
Really?

315
00:17:26,950 --> 00:17:30,120
We might get delivery orders
while we're out for lunch,

316
00:17:30,420 --> 00:17:31,920
and that would just be my loss.

317
00:17:32,220 --> 00:17:33,820
Who am I to complain...

318
00:17:33,890 --> 00:17:36,230
when I get delicious
home-cooked meals every day?

319
00:17:37,460 --> 00:17:38,500
Boss,

320
00:17:38,560 --> 00:17:40,500
I really want to be
a full-time employee here.

321
00:17:41,930 --> 00:17:43,570
A person needs to have a future.

322
00:17:43,630 --> 00:17:45,200
What's the point
of working full-time...

323
00:17:45,270 --> 00:17:46,700
at a small cafe like this?

324
00:17:48,810 --> 00:17:51,580
Don't you have
any life plans or goals?

325
00:17:52,740 --> 00:17:55,180
- Of course I do.
- What are they?

326
00:17:56,610 --> 00:17:59,380
Living happily day by day.

327
00:17:59,880 --> 00:18:02,520
What kind of goal is that?
Is that really your life goal?

328
00:18:03,490 --> 00:18:05,620
You have no idea
how important that is.

329
00:18:06,990 --> 00:18:08,690
Over time,
I realized life is all about...

330
00:18:09,230 --> 00:18:11,160
getting caught up
in unexpected things,

331
00:18:11,230 --> 00:18:13,230
getting entangled,
and getting stabbed in the back.

332
00:18:13,930 --> 00:18:14,930
Every time that happened,

333
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:17,670
my desire to live happily
grew desperate.

334
00:18:18,700 --> 00:18:21,370
So, rather than becoming
something right now,

335
00:18:21,810 --> 00:18:22,810
my top priority...

336
00:18:23,070 --> 00:18:25,480
is to live happily...

337
00:18:25,710 --> 00:18:28,110
in the present moment today.

338
00:18:29,210 --> 00:18:30,380
Just look.

339
00:18:30,750 --> 00:18:33,380
Thanks to you,
I cleared my mission today.

340
00:18:33,980 --> 00:18:35,520
With this delicious packed meal,

341
00:18:35,520 --> 00:18:37,490
my mission to be happy today
is complete.

342
00:18:41,760 --> 00:18:43,090
One, two.

343
00:18:45,600 --> 00:18:48,830
(Grand Opening)

344
00:18:52,840 --> 00:18:55,040
To all the distinguished guests...

345
00:18:55,110 --> 00:18:58,080
who attended the first store opening
of the Shoejoy brand,

346
00:18:58,140 --> 00:18:59,540
which will lead
the future of Cheongma,

347
00:18:59,610 --> 00:19:01,650
I sincerely thank you.

348
00:19:01,650 --> 00:19:03,410
Please feel free to look around.

349
00:19:03,910 --> 00:19:07,080
If you need anything,
please find our staff.

350
00:19:07,150 --> 00:19:08,320
Thank you.

351
00:19:28,370 --> 00:19:31,240
What is the core feature
of the Shoejoy brand?

352
00:19:33,640 --> 00:19:35,180
Creating products
that support the foot arch...

353
00:19:35,250 --> 00:19:37,680
and use magnetic
push-and-pull properties...

354
00:19:37,750 --> 00:19:42,120
to promote healthy walking posture
is the core of our brand.

355
00:19:42,920 --> 00:19:44,990
Do you have any future plans?

356
00:19:45,590 --> 00:19:47,090
Building on the technology
I mentioned earlier,

357
00:19:47,160 --> 00:19:48,760
Shoejoy will then
incorporate design.

358
00:19:48,830 --> 00:19:51,190
To directly manage this technology,

359
00:19:51,260 --> 00:19:53,700
we guarantee quality
with full domestic production.

360
00:19:53,760 --> 00:19:55,230
Driven by
our exceptional technology,

361
00:19:55,300 --> 00:19:57,470
we ensure proper posture
and healthy steps for everyone,

362
00:19:57,530 --> 00:19:59,340
regardless of age or gender,

363
00:19:59,400 --> 00:20:03,240
as we grow into
a global brand trusted worldwide.

364
00:20:03,540 --> 00:20:05,180
Thank you for the interview today.

365
00:20:05,240 --> 00:20:06,240
- Thank you.
- Right.

366
00:20:07,640 --> 00:20:09,410
Chief Cha's pretty impressive.

367
00:20:09,410 --> 00:20:12,450
For a new brand,
the response is quite good.

368
00:20:13,180 --> 00:20:15,550
See, what did I tell you?

369
00:20:15,990 --> 00:20:18,660
He is exactly like you
when you were young.

370
00:20:21,790 --> 00:20:24,230
Dad, isn't Seok Jin awesome?

371
00:20:24,390 --> 00:20:27,260
For a prospective son-in-law,
I think he's above average.

372
00:20:28,630 --> 00:20:32,640
Above average?
We'll have to wait and see.

373
00:20:38,380 --> 00:20:41,110
The points Chief Cha barely earned,

374
00:20:41,180 --> 00:20:44,250
it seems you're losing them all
with your own mouth.

375
00:20:44,410 --> 00:20:46,080
I need to hype him up
to Dad like this.

376
00:20:46,080 --> 00:20:49,890
Chief Cha is doing well enough
on his own,

377
00:20:49,950 --> 00:20:53,560
so just stay by his side
and wait patiently.

378
00:21:02,630 --> 00:21:06,040
Our products are sized...

379
00:21:22,520 --> 00:21:24,590
Excuse me, is this...

380
00:21:25,060 --> 00:21:27,120
where Joo Ae Sook lives?

381
00:21:27,120 --> 00:21:28,160
What?

382
00:21:29,360 --> 00:21:31,230
- Ae Sook?
- That's right.

383
00:21:31,960 --> 00:21:34,230
Would it be possible to meet her?

384
00:21:34,230 --> 00:21:37,100
How can you talk to someone
who's passed away?

385
00:21:37,570 --> 00:21:40,870
- What?
- Ae Sook died three years ago.

386
00:21:41,940 --> 00:21:44,640
She passed away?

387
00:21:44,640 --> 00:21:46,010
She ran up...

388
00:21:46,580 --> 00:21:49,280
all the debt she could at every bar.

389
00:21:50,580 --> 00:21:51,850
Then three years ago,

390
00:21:52,450 --> 00:21:54,480
she died of alcoholism.

391
00:21:56,290 --> 00:21:58,460
It has been years since she died,

392
00:21:59,090 --> 00:22:01,690
but debt collectors
still come by sometimes.

393
00:22:02,260 --> 00:22:03,260
If she had any family,

394
00:22:03,330 --> 00:22:05,530
they say they'd collect
all that money,

395
00:22:05,960 --> 00:22:07,760
making such a fuss.

396
00:22:08,330 --> 00:22:11,370
But I doubt she had a family.

397
00:22:12,400 --> 00:22:14,740
She was alone her whole life.

398
00:22:16,040 --> 00:22:18,380
Actually, when she was young,

399
00:22:19,580 --> 00:22:22,450
I think she gave birth
to a daughter.

400
00:22:25,420 --> 00:22:26,550
Anyway...

401
00:22:27,250 --> 00:22:28,490
How do you know...

402
00:22:30,890 --> 00:22:33,820
that good-for-nothing Ae Sook?

403
00:22:36,090 --> 00:22:38,630
Actually, I don't. Take care.

404
00:22:46,200 --> 00:22:47,740
You took care of it, right?

405
00:22:47,900 --> 00:22:52,780
Yes, of course.
I mean, I'm quite the actor.

406
00:22:52,840 --> 00:22:56,110
As soon as I told him that creditors
were still chasing her for money,

407
00:22:56,110 --> 00:22:59,120
he took off without a second glance.

408
00:22:59,750 --> 00:23:00,820
As expected,

409
00:23:00,880 --> 00:23:03,590
scaring people with money
works like a charm.

410
00:23:04,350 --> 00:23:07,990
- Are you sure they won't come back?
- Absolutely.

411
00:23:08,330 --> 00:23:12,160
They won't even come near the place.
Don't you worry.

412
00:23:13,560 --> 00:23:15,470
I sent the payment,
so check your account.

413
00:23:16,670 --> 00:23:17,830
Right.

414
00:23:19,400 --> 00:23:23,210
Got it. I've confirmed the deposit.

415
00:23:23,910 --> 00:23:26,810
You're keeping a close eye
on An Guk Cheol, right?

416
00:23:26,880 --> 00:23:28,450
Of course.

417
00:23:29,050 --> 00:23:31,410
Even today, I followed him all day.

418
00:23:32,220 --> 00:23:34,620
If anything unusual comes up,
I will immediately...

419
00:23:35,120 --> 00:23:37,220
report it to you.

420
00:23:37,720 --> 00:23:38,720
I will.

421
00:23:40,660 --> 00:23:41,760
Oh, boy.

422
00:23:42,190 --> 00:23:44,800
I had all the winning numbers
down to the last digit,

423
00:23:44,830 --> 00:23:46,560
but when I checked...

424
00:23:46,560 --> 00:23:48,270
Unbelievable.

425
00:23:48,330 --> 00:23:50,800
The lottery ticket
was dated last year.

426
00:23:51,230 --> 00:23:54,740
Oh, what a waste.

427
00:23:59,380 --> 00:24:00,380
Wait.

428
00:24:01,310 --> 00:24:03,980
Even if I didn't win the lottery,

429
00:24:05,150 --> 00:24:07,180
I should at least
get a pension out of it.

430
00:24:07,580 --> 00:24:09,150
Yeah, that's right.

431
00:24:10,490 --> 00:24:13,520
I should get a regular pension,
and at least make some profit.

432
00:24:16,130 --> 00:24:18,460
- I'm home.
- Hey, you're home.

433
00:24:19,060 --> 00:24:20,830
Come and have a seat.

434
00:24:25,540 --> 00:24:27,240
Do you have something to say?

435
00:24:28,340 --> 00:24:29,610
So,

436
00:24:30,670 --> 00:24:33,310
how much do you make a month?

437
00:24:33,810 --> 00:24:34,850
What?

438
00:24:35,150 --> 00:24:38,650
I mean, out of what you earn,
just give me 60...

439
00:24:39,280 --> 00:24:41,150
Give me 60 percent of it.

440
00:24:41,890 --> 00:24:43,150
Grandma.

441
00:24:43,220 --> 00:24:45,420
What is it? Can't you do it?

442
00:24:47,060 --> 00:24:50,690
Sixty percent is too much.
I have to pay rent for this place.

443
00:24:51,190 --> 00:24:54,130
I'm already giving you money
for living expenses too.

444
00:24:54,130 --> 00:24:56,570
I'm saying this because
what you're giving me isn't enough.

445
00:24:57,130 --> 00:25:00,640
Anyway, that's how it'll be.
Exactly 60 percent. Got it?

446
00:25:09,110 --> 00:25:10,650
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

447
00:25:11,650 --> 00:25:15,020
Hey, are you free this weekend
by any chance?

448
00:25:15,750 --> 00:25:16,750
What?

449
00:25:17,020 --> 00:25:20,620
It's just that my mother
really wants to see you.

450
00:25:21,360 --> 00:25:22,590
Me?

451
00:25:22,830 --> 00:25:25,760
Yes, she finished her coloring book,

452
00:25:26,130 --> 00:25:28,670
and she wants to show it to you.
Also...

453
00:25:29,770 --> 00:25:32,400
Well, she really wants
to spend time with you.

454
00:25:34,870 --> 00:25:36,540
It's probably uncomfortable
for you, right?

455
00:25:37,670 --> 00:25:39,980
Actually, I'd love that.

456
00:25:40,280 --> 00:25:43,250
I got her
some new colored pencils anyway.

457
00:25:43,250 --> 00:25:46,350
They apply smoothly
and draw really well.

458
00:25:46,450 --> 00:25:47,550
Right.

459
00:25:47,920 --> 00:25:49,420
My mom will love them.

460
00:25:52,420 --> 00:25:53,690
By the way,

461
00:25:54,060 --> 00:25:57,130
you'll be there with us, right?

462
00:25:57,130 --> 00:25:59,430
What? Yes, of course.

463
00:25:59,500 --> 00:26:01,830
Just in case something happens
to my mom again.

464
00:26:02,530 --> 00:26:05,340
Sounds good. Anytime works for me.

465
00:26:06,500 --> 00:26:07,500
Thanks.

466
00:26:09,910 --> 00:26:11,840
Are you really thankful?

467
00:26:16,780 --> 00:26:19,480
That's enough
for the formal interview.

468
00:26:19,750 --> 00:26:23,220
Do you have anything else to add?
Perhaps a pledge or final thought.

469
00:26:27,820 --> 00:26:28,930
I've always respected you...

470
00:26:28,990 --> 00:26:30,660
since I was at the orphanage.

471
00:26:31,090 --> 00:26:34,530
I will work hard by your side
so that no one at Cheongma...

472
00:26:34,600 --> 00:26:36,430
can threaten your position.

473
00:26:37,870 --> 00:26:38,900
Okay.

474
00:26:39,100 --> 00:26:40,740
The secretary's office
will contact you.

475
00:26:49,280 --> 00:26:50,280
Thank you.

476
00:27:12,070 --> 00:27:13,070
Thank you.

477
00:27:14,640 --> 00:27:15,640
What the...

478
00:27:29,120 --> 00:27:31,320
What? Did it stop?

479
00:27:33,190 --> 00:27:37,060
Hello?
There are people in here. Hello?

480
00:27:37,390 --> 00:27:39,200
The elevator stopped!

481
00:27:45,070 --> 00:27:46,100
Hold on a second.

482
00:27:46,840 --> 00:27:48,100
Let me try.

483
00:27:51,610 --> 00:27:54,240
We apologize. Please wait a moment.

484
00:27:54,410 --> 00:27:56,150
The repair technician
will be there shortly.

485
00:27:56,210 --> 00:27:58,310
Right. Please fix it
as soon as possible.

486
00:28:07,420 --> 00:28:11,960
This is so annoying.
Why did it have to stop right now?

487
00:28:24,210 --> 00:28:27,040
If you need this,
feel free to use it.

488
00:28:43,590 --> 00:28:45,030
(Cheongma Foundation
Job Application: Choi Jun Hwan)

489
00:28:45,960 --> 00:28:47,560
- You're here.
- Hey.

490
00:28:47,830 --> 00:28:49,200
Did anyone interview with you today?

491
00:28:50,400 --> 00:28:53,800
Yes, it's been frustrating
without a secretary.

492
00:28:54,370 --> 00:28:56,810
I think this guy is pretty good.

493
00:28:57,140 --> 00:28:58,610
How can you tell just from a resume?

494
00:28:58,610 --> 00:29:01,080
You know, it's just a feeling.

495
00:29:01,340 --> 00:29:03,710
- He seems all right.
- Well, he wasn't bad.

496
00:29:03,710 --> 00:29:05,120
He seems to think quick on his feet.

497
00:29:05,780 --> 00:29:07,120
I thought so too.

498
00:29:08,380 --> 00:29:09,720
Have you met him in person?

499
00:29:10,820 --> 00:29:12,260
No, of course not.

500
00:29:12,920 --> 00:29:14,820
Anyway, go with him.

501
00:29:14,820 --> 00:29:17,530
He might turn out to be
someone I need.

502
00:29:18,460 --> 00:29:22,030
That could be true.
Okay, I'll keep that in mind.

503
00:29:25,200 --> 00:29:28,100
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

504
00:29:30,240 --> 00:29:31,540
That ring...

505
00:29:34,510 --> 00:29:37,310
It isn't very pretty.
Could you not wear it?

506
00:29:45,220 --> 00:29:46,260
Eat up.

507
00:29:46,290 --> 00:29:47,820
You should dig in too.

508
00:29:51,830 --> 00:29:54,700
Do you prefer flour or rice tteok
in your tteokbokki?

509
00:29:56,530 --> 00:29:57,600
- I...
- Wait.

510
00:29:58,500 --> 00:30:00,200
Let's say it together on three.

511
00:30:01,240 --> 00:30:03,340
- One, two, three. Wheat.
- Wheat.

512
00:30:06,840 --> 00:30:08,950
Tteokbokki is definitely better
with flour tteok.

513
00:30:10,710 --> 00:30:13,020
Next, jjajangmyeon or jjamppong.

514
00:30:13,080 --> 00:30:14,680
- 1, 2, 3. Jjajang.
- Jjajang.

515
00:30:15,620 --> 00:30:16,620
Jjajangmyeon rules.

516
00:30:40,580 --> 00:30:41,740
Right here.

517
00:30:43,950 --> 00:30:46,120
Do I have something on my face?

518
00:30:49,820 --> 00:30:50,820
You're good now.

519
00:31:05,540 --> 00:31:08,940
Mom, I got a mosquito bite.
Where's the ointment?

520
00:31:09,410 --> 00:31:11,210
You need to be extra careful,

521
00:31:11,270 --> 00:31:13,210
especially
with your mosquito allergy.

522
00:31:14,240 --> 00:31:16,080
Let me see, come here.

523
00:31:16,680 --> 00:31:18,920
Oh, my. Goodness.

524
00:31:19,480 --> 00:31:22,220
This is going to swell up.

525
00:31:22,290 --> 00:31:24,620
What if it fills with pus
like last time?

526
00:31:24,690 --> 00:31:26,790
- I'll get the ointment.
- Sure.

527
00:31:27,620 --> 00:31:28,930
Unbelievable.

528
00:31:28,990 --> 00:31:31,660
Who on earth does she take after?

529
00:31:31,730 --> 00:31:34,200
No one else in the family
is like this.

530
00:31:34,260 --> 00:31:37,600
Whatever. I'm annoyed too.
Gosh, it itches.

531
00:31:37,670 --> 00:31:38,670
Don't scratch it.

532
00:31:38,740 --> 00:31:40,470
Should we just see a doctor?

533
00:31:41,100 --> 00:31:42,670
Oh, dear.

534
00:31:45,140 --> 00:31:46,310
Darn it.

535
00:31:55,920 --> 00:31:56,920
Darn.

536
00:31:58,660 --> 00:32:00,660
Darn mosquitoes are everywhere.

537
00:32:30,720 --> 00:32:34,620
(A Trap Called Desire)

538
00:32:34,690 --> 00:32:38,060
You must've been upset that I wanted
to look for my biological mother.

539
00:32:38,130 --> 00:32:40,160
You're like a curse, aren't you?

540
00:32:40,230 --> 00:32:42,530
Are my words a joke?
Is your husband a joke to you?

541
00:32:42,600 --> 00:32:45,230
I honestly feel like I don't take
after either Mom or Dad.

542
00:32:45,300 --> 00:32:46,370
You do.

543
00:32:46,440 --> 00:32:49,040
You seem to care too much
about what others think.

544
00:32:49,110 --> 00:32:51,240
My father was never like that.

545
00:32:51,310 --> 00:32:52,940
Are you judging people
by their backgrounds...

546
00:32:53,010 --> 00:32:54,010
and sorting them into classes, too?

547
00:32:54,010 --> 00:32:55,040
Why did you take off your ring?

548
00:32:55,110 --> 00:32:56,680
Is Ko Eun Seol the reason
you're not wearing it?

549
00:32:56,680 --> 00:32:59,120
She likes you,
and that's been affecting you.

550
00:32:59,180 --> 00:33:00,180
Ko Eun Seol.

551
00:33:00,920 --> 00:33:02,520
Secretary Choi,
you need to be different.

552
00:33:02,520 --> 00:33:05,460
You must only think about
what benefits and harms me.

553
00:33:06,190 --> 00:33:08,190
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
